From 885d31c9f4cc5b67aa6ad704b95e5152215ec404 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mempool: implement the sharded UTXO spent filter

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
The original split preserved source semantics; candidate repairs below complete
the missing prerequisite/build ownership.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Fast-path single-input CheckRegularTransaction duplicate-input checks,
coalesce BlockUndo disk writes, and optimize bulk mempool clear.

Original-Commit: a4ea86865414bbf4f98512bbd4460e2a42897acc
Original-Patch: ecash/020
Split-Concern: filter

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Repair: Import the matching filter header from later41 and compile
the implementation here rather than at later38. Add direct growth, duplicate,
erase, Bloom rebuild and clear lifecycle coverage. Compact fingerprints are
advisory hints, never UTXO validity proofs. Mempool consumer integration stays
with its actual owner; remove later duplicate header/build additions.

